  "scientific_scope": "Stage-2.2C trains the Stage-2.2B visual front end for 30,000 trials on a moderate nuisance curriculum: continuous position jitter, moderate per-dot brightness asymmetry, modest total-area variation, and mixed ordinary/closer spacing. Frozen OOD tests then exceed that envelope with held-out half-grid phase, much stronger two-dot brightness asymmetry, and a combined position/area/spacing/brightness shift. Total signal-energy remains identically distributed for 1 and 2, and total-area distributions are identical for 1 and 2 within each profile. OOD blocks receive zero plastic updates. No object count, peak count, or target-derived numerosity feature is injected; FlyWire coordinates remain visualization-only.",
  "note": "This run validates the reward-learning protocol. It is not yet evidence that the full FlyWire connectome learned numerosity."
